# Stream a turn's speech as it is generated, instead of only at turn_end.
#
# The tts produces frames throughout a turn, but the wav is written once, at the
# end -- and the end comes after the drain, which is the longest phase there is.
# Measured with the Q8_0 build:
#
#     turn loop      5.8 - 10.3 s
#     tts drain      3.6 -  6.7 s   (generating 10-18 s of speech)
#
# So a driver hears nothing for the whole of both, then the entire answer at
# once. The speech for the first words existed seconds earlier.
#
# This adds `--stream-audio N` (serve mode only): every N finished frames are
# decoded and emitted as an `audio_delta` event carrying a wav path, and the
# remainder is flushed just before `turn_end`. N=8 is ~640 ms.
#
# It needs no new state beyond a cursor, because voicechat_tts_write_wav already
# decodes a few frames of causal run-up before `first` and discards them -- so
# consecutive ranges join without a seam, which is exactly what the existing
# mid-session trim relies on.
#
# `--stream-dir` says where the chunk wavs go; /tmp is a tmpfs in the container
# and the driver unlinks each one after reading it. With N=0 (the default)
# nothing changes, so one-shot `--audio`/`--tts-out` and the existing serve
# protocol are untouched.
#
# Against sansamour/llama-voicechat.cpp @ f45001fc (branch voicechat).

